</div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1488888-did-any-of-you-see-the-trailer-for-the-remake-of-anne-rices-s-interview-with-the-vampire?p=1489220#post1489220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've rarely seen the usual suspects as defenders. Hatewatching and tubing is where the real money is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I should have made it clearer I mean they'll be attacking the show for casting a black actor as the very very white Louis which will naturally force a defence from more socially concessions quarter regardless of it the show is good. (I'm still trying to figure how I ended up defending the star trek discovery from some misogynist neckbeard In the pub last month considering I think it's crap)<br /> <br /> The only time I think I've seen them 'defend' was joker and cyberpunk which were attacked by the evil woke femminazis such as myself. Even though I quite liked joker and thought cyberpunk was 'alright' once it got patched.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1488888-did-any-of-you-see-the-trailer-for-the-remake-of-anne-rices-s-interview-with-the-vampire?p=1489235#post1489235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's enough of a business model that there's no way of knowing how sincere any of the tubers even are. At least some are likely just playing to the audience.</div> </div> </div> </div>Almost certainly, some of then can't be as upset by some shitty show as they come across. I'm not even convinced anyone on 'my' side actually liked the 2016 ghostbusters movie so a lot of then must be pandering.<br /> <br /> Although I'll conceed No Bullshit is almost certainly just ferociously stupid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 08-05-2022, 04:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-05T14:19:51-07:00","id":1489270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1488888-did-any-of-you-see-the-trailer-for-the-remake-of-anne-rices-s-interview-with-the-vampire?p=1489247#post1489247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My next question is why a remake?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The terminology around these discussions generally makes them harder to have.<br /> <br /> This isn't, strictly speaking, a remake. It's not a remake of the 1994 movie, because it's a TV show that's ignoring the changes made in that movie and going back to the 1976 book as it's base source. Calling it an adaption of a book is a better way of approaching it because... that's what it is. It's looking at a 46 year old story, and adapting it to a different medium and updating some stuff for a modern audience. The just also happens to be a popular movie made on the same source material.<br /> <br /> Let's also remember it's been 28 years since the movie came out. There are people that have been born, graduated university, and gotten their first career oriented job since the movie was released. A whole generation between the last major adaptation of the books and this adaptation of the books is a big stretch to treat as excessive.<br /> <br /> And of course, why? Because money. We live in a capitalist society (however any of us feel about that and however strongly). AMC is an adaptation juggernaut. Their highly successful adaptations have helped fuel a bunch of highly successful original programming as well. Profiting off of successful adaptations gives them the bank accounts to take risks on a lot of shows that other TV studios might take a pass on, or would get paywalled into premium channels/proprietary streaming services. To paraphrase Robert Downy Jr. to Chris Evans (who is very vocal about how much he dislikes big budget Hollywood studio movies): You play Captain America, you make him the best version of him he can be under the MCU leadership team, and then you have all the money you want to do whatever indie projects you want to do; which more people will watch because the guy that plays Captain America is in them.<br /> <br /> We don't get TV shows like Mad Men, Breaking Bad/Better Call Saul, and other extremely well received shows from AMC without them also doing things like The Walking Dead.<br /> <br /> HBO creatives on some of their smaller cool shows frequently joked about getting &quot;that dragon money,&quot; because when HBO was flush during the height of GoT's success, HBO green-lit a bunch of smaller stuff they might have passed on in leaner times, and gave them the budgets they needed to really shine.<br /> <br /> Dislike the system all you want, but it's the system these people have to operate in. They need big franchise money as their core income. That means finding big existing properties to put their spin on. That's why remakes/reboots/reimaginings/new adaptations have <u>always</u> been part of the business. Dragonball, one of the largest animation juggernauts in the world, started as yet another retelling of Journey to the West, which is one of the most retold stories in existence. The majority of Shakespeare's players are not original works, as they're either retellings of historical events, or retellings of previous fiction other people did first. When the US film industry took off, they remade moves all the time.<br /> <br /> Retelling popular stories is such a default mode of human culture, and cuts across all cultures, that the question shouldn't be &quot;why a remake?&quot; but, &quot;why has it taken this long to get a new version of this?&quot; In pretty much every culture on Earth, once fixed forms of a story (novels, scripts, etc.) are introduced, adaptations to other media and remakes start happening. We have ~500 years of history to attest to this. <br /> <br /> This isn't to say the new stories don't deserve a chance too, but the reactionary movement against retelling older stories is very new, and mostly brought on by the digital age and much easier access to older versions of the story. The reason people are so burnt out on remakes today is that we live in an age where we actually have easy access to the originals and all the retellings made since, so it feels saturated. Twenty years ago, the difficulty in trying to binge watch every retelling of A Christmas Carol would have been finding copies of all of them, now it's mostly finding the time to watch them all as the movies alone would equate to something like 50 hours. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Surely there must be other books and legends about the undead that could have been adapted for films. </div> </div> </div>Again: this is a new adaptation of the novels for TV. They're also hoping to adapt a huge amount of Rice's books that have never actually been adapted at all (there's a lot of books in the Vampire Chronicles and it's witches spin off).<br /> <br /> And since this is a TV studio making TV, that means they're not taking up space in a movie studio's production budget for doing a new vampires story, or adapting a less known one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I know there is a huge amount of manga books that deal with vampires and even horror writers like Bentley Little did a take on the genre years ago that was interesting and he burrowed from Chinese lore. </div> </div> </div>I believe I've made this point in the recent past already: manga gets adapted to other media all the time. If you want to watch some cool manga inspired shows about vampires, there's a bunch of anime out there for you to consume already, and thanks to the streaming era it's more accessible to non-Japanese audiences than ever.<br /> <br /> If you think retellings are generally badly received... ask manga/anime fans what they feel about live action adaptations (even ones done in Japan).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1488888-did-any-of-you-see-the-trailer-for-the-remake-of-anne-rices-s-interview-with-the-vampire?p=1489262#post1489262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not even convinced 'my' side actually liked the 2016 ghostbusters movie so a lot of then must be pandering.</div> </div> </div> </div>I liked it. Not a great movie, but a decent one that that received criticism well in excess of its flaws. It was fun, I don't regret seeing it, but I'm not going out of my way to rewatch it either.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-05T15:44:34-07:00","id":1489274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1488888-did-any-of-you-see-the-trailer-for-the-remake-of-anne-rices-s-interview-with-the-vampire?p=1489270#post1489270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The terminology around these discussions generally makes them harder to have.<br /> <br /> I liked it. Not a great movie, but a decent one that that received criticism well in excess of its flaws. It was fun, I don't regret seeing it, but I'm not going out of my way to rewatch it either.</div> </div> </div> </div>I chuckled at Kate mckinnon's &quot;womp womp&quot; line I think lesley Jones did something which made me giggle. It also made me accidently snicker when my big commie gf started getting snarky about product placement. Having never eaten papa John's her animated ranting/explanation about the generic cups was fun. <br /> <br /> Its my go to example of corporate sterility in film. Being both a pointless remake and failed franchise launcher. I'd use mummy but nobody i know watched it<br /> <br /> Then again ghostbuster 2 was pretty forgettable and I havnt watched afterlife.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 08-05-2022, 06:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-06T19:00:05-07:00","id":1489380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1488888-did-any-of-you-see-the-trailer-for-the-remake-of-anne-rices-s-interview-with-the-vampire?p=1489068#post1489068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Trying to convince AMC to not change things in adapting to TV (and they're not actually part of Hollywood) is pointless because they've made a shit ton of money doing it. AMC's adaptations are frequently very popular with fans despite (and sometime because of) changes to the source material.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is why I couldn't really stomach Preacher. I wanted to like it, I loved the cast and the production looked pretty good, but with the slowness of season one and completely missing the characterisation of the core trio I just couldn't keep watching it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1488888-did-any-of-you-see-the-trailer-for-the-remake-of-anne-rices-s-interview-with-the-vampire?p=1489218#post1489218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Much like the Watchmen TV show helped bring the history of black people in Tusla back into the public consciousness (both the good and bad parts of that history), this could be used to include a part of New Orleans history that's rarely touched upon in live-action fiction.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the other hand this was an adaptation which I really enjoyed and felt it worked really well, and the changes they made to reinforce the new story they were trying to tell really worked for me. That's HBO Max, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-06T19:24:39-07:00","id":1489382,"title":"","content":"Watchmen was a sequel rather than an adaptation.<br /> <br /> I will state that it fundamentally DISAGREES with Alan Moore on superheroes being an extension of white power fantasies, though.<br /> <br /> Moore, being a brit, doesn't seem to realize that African Americans have their own tradition of their own folk heroes and vigilantes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-06T20:51:38-07:00","id":1489388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1488888-did-any-of-you-see-the-trailer-for-the-remake-of-anne-rices-s-interview-with-the-vampire?p=1489382#post1489382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Watchmen was a sequel rather than an adaptation.<br /> <br /> I will state that it fundamentally DISAGREES with Alan Moore on superheroes being an extension of white power fantasies, though.<br /> <br /> Moore, being a brit, doesn't seem to realize that African Americans have their own tradition of their own folk heroes and vigilantes.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hell, every country has stuff like that. Many Japanese folktales and in things like Kabuki theatre are stories of folk heroes or members of low ranking samurai families looking to right wrongs or protect the common folk. Many superhero films and comics built upwards out of cowboy movies, which themselves were often inspired by Japanese samurai movies and were themselves inspired by Japanese folktales and theatre. And then you have an equally long history of similar stories about vigilantes who right wrongs with magical or superhuman ability coming from China and India.<br /> <br /> Even the earliest comic books like Superman were more about class struggle and fighting against corrupt politicians, land and business owners than anything related to race (though many of the characters in these early comics were write). Now certainly, some superheroes are extensions of white power fantasies or have been adopted into white power fantasies (the Punisher is a good example) but yeah, I don't think Alan Moore was really correct in that assertion that superheroes were something unique to western, white society or being an extension of white power fantasies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-07T00:33:16-07:00","id":1489399,"title":"","content":"Moore misses how race-obsessed Lovecraft was, as well; his &quot;Neonomicon&quot; treats it like a footnote at most and focuses on trying to shoehorn the source material into his own sexual peccadilloes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11599,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","user":"Reasor","date":". 08-07-2022, 03:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-11T02:02:55-07:00","id":1489725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1488888-did-any-of-you-see-the-trailer-for-the-remake-of-anne-rices-s-interview-with-the-vampire?p=1489218#post1489218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Much like the Watchmen TV show helped bring the history of black people in Tusla back into the public consciousness (both the good and bad parts of that history), this could be used to include a part of New Orleans history that's rarely touched upon in live-action fiction.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty Baby is a pretty infamous movie about that part of history that starred Susan Sarandon and a 12 year old Brooke Shield. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-11T03:47:20-07:00","id":1489727,"title":"","content":"&quot;Rarely&quot; not &quot;never&quot; touched upon. We can probably aim for better than &quot;infamous.&quot; Also not making it mostly about white people given the Treme district's historical connection with fee black people, and Storyville being a heavily integrated area of the city where a lot of modern New Orleans culture was born where people where allowed to ignore the social norms that separated cultures in the rest of the city (and country for much of its history). The fact that the biggest movie you can think of (and it's not really your fault here) is 46 years old is also part of my point here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-01T09:21:03-07:00","id":1494091,"title":"","content":"I saw the first episode yesterday, it's pretty good so far","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-08T16:19:44-07:00","id":1494630,"title":"","content":"first 2 episodes were good. like really good. i really didnt expect it to be this good after seeing how they butchered the lore. But somehow they have created a great show that stands on its own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24527,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24527-blackshade","user":"blackshade","date":". 10-08-2022, 08:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24527-blackshade","name":"blackshade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-11T10:20:24-07:00","id":1494795,"title":"","content":"Being a purist when it comes to lore I'll probably not bother with the series at all. If it's not broke why &quot;fix&quot; it is my belief when it comes to my favorite stories as a child","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-11T15:05:43-07:00","id":1494812,"title":"","content":"The idea of being a &quot;purist&quot; for the lore of a non-interactive form of media boggles my mind. Being a purist about RPG lore? OK, I can get that, RPGs are a collaborative media and being a purist about lore is a good way to keep the group on the same page about things.<br /> <br /> Being a purist about novels just reduces the number of novels in the world. Most novels are the product of someone saying, &quot;I really love story X, but I want to do my version of it instead.&quot; Even people like Tolkien had that as a motivation for all his world building: he wanted to take old stories from his younger years and do his own spin on them. Shakespeare's plays are full of retellings of older stories originally done by someone else. Etc. <br /> <br /> Reworking old stories into new contexts and new perspectives is an essential part of art and culture. Why deny yourself the chance to enjoy old stories anew as someone else takes a stab at them?<br /> <br /> Even more so when we're talking about an adaptation from novel to TV show, where changes from the source material were always going to be necessary because novels aren't screenplays designed to be read on their own and to be directly adapted to film/TV/etc.<br /> <br /> It's fine to say, &quot;I have a lot of nostalgia for the older version, but little interest in new material in the same IP, so I'm not going to bother.&quot; It has nothing to do with some sort of artistic &quot;purity&quot; that older versions supposedly have (which they didn't because they're always knocking off something else anyway).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-11T17:41:04-07:00","id":1494825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1488888-did-any-of-you-see-the-trailer-for-the-remake-of-anne-rices-s-interview-with-the-vampire?p=1494812#post1494812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea of being a &quot;purist&quot; for the lore of a non-interactive form of media boggles my mind. Being a purist about RPG lore? OK, I can get that, RPGs are a collaborative media and being a purist about lore is a good way to keep the group on the same page about things.</div> </div> </div> </div>On my end, it's more like the fact that I don't understand why they keep changing stuff while claiming to like the material. The Vampire Chronicles deserve to have a faithful adaptation and every episode is more and more changes that aren't remotely similar to the characters in the books.<br /> <br /> If you're going to do a Louis who loves Lestat, isn't guilty about murder, and tortured by being a monster then why even call Interview with a Vampire?<br /> <br /> Why do you think you can do better than the author?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-11T19:19:01-07:00","id":1494829,"title":"","content":"I watched the first episode. It feels like they wanted to do their own original vampire story but felt that they would get more money or funding by using the Interview With the Vampire name. They're doing the bare minimum to lift stuff from the novel and I would prefer it if it was just its own thing entirely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-11T20:14:27-07:00","id":1494832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1488888-did-any-of-you-see-the-trailer-for-the-remake-of-anne-rices-s-interview-with-the-vampire?p=1494825#post1494825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On my end, it's more like the fact that I don't understand why they keep changing stuff while claiming to like the material.</div> </div> </div> </div>Every spend time with fanfic writers? Because... that's exactly what fanfic is all about<b></b>: loving something so much you want to write your own version of it, which changes you would think would expand it in a fashion you think other fans would like.<br /> <br /> Fanfic starts with &quot;fan&quot; for a reason. It's not haterfic.<br /> <br /> It might not be your scene... it isn't my scene... but I know enough fanfic people that clearly love their fandoms, and then rewrite those stories all over the place.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Vampire Chronicles deserve to have a faithful adaptation and every episode is more and more changes that aren't remotely similar to the characters in the books. </div> </div> </div>Why does it deserve anything? It's a set of novels that already got published and made Rice a lot of money. It probably can't get a direct adaptation because... the original books are actually not great for adaptation without significant alteration. Also Rice doesn't like a lot of the early stuff in it anymore and might want some changes and this is the closest she can get to signing off to her equivalent of Lucas's edit to the original SW trilogy. GRRM approved the ending of GoT... that didn't really make fans happier with it..<br /> <br /> &quot;Faithful&quot; is always subjective (is the MCU faithful to the comics because it's faithful to the spirit of the characters, or unfaithful for taking huge liberties with the source material?).<br /> <br /> [quote]If you're going to do a Louis who loves Lestat, isn't guilty about murder, and tortured by being a monster then why even call Interview<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> with a Vampire? </div> </div> </div>Louis loves Lestat on some level the whole time in the novels, he just eventually figures out how toxic their relationship is, he gets over needing to kill the feed quicker in the book than the movie, and according to Lestat, Louis completely self-aggrandized his story in the first novel too make himself sound like the good one of their relationship and play down all the stuff they did together.<br /> <br /> We basically got the adaptation you seem to want already: the film, that played in this direction harder than the original book did (you know, they changed stuff).<br /> <br /> AnubisXy's complaint? That I understand. Even if that's not what really happened, we've had so many things where an original story gets shoved into a franchise for sales purposes and we can tell, that you don't want to come off feeling that way whether it's just how you're handling changes, or because that's really what you're doing.<br /> <br /> Pretty much all of Gen X and Millenials (Zoomers might not quite be there yet) have had some experience with &quot;slap [franchise label] on this original story and we'll double profits, so screw new titles!&quot; and seen how it only made things worse. It's a critique about a specific feeling the show is giving off, not a flat complaint about &quot;change for the sake of change,&quot; when change is inherent in adaptations.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why do you think you can do better than the author? </div> </div> </div>1) Most present authors think they can do better than the past versions of themselves. So I have trouble with any assumption that authors are inherently infallible here and you can't actually change for the better. Stephen King is notoriously snarky about film adaptations of his work, because he knows they're going to change stuff he doesn't think should get changed. However, when a change gets made that he likes? He's effusive in his praise. Because yeah, it does happen. The ending of The Mist is probably the most famous example, where he's been quoted as wishing he'd come up with that ending instead of the original.<br /> <br /> So it's not really unreasonable to think that the original author can't be questioned about these things.<br /> <br /> 2) When it comes to adaptations? Frequently original authors don't understand the new medium and want to keep or change things that don't really work that way. The GoT point above is a great example. I'm pretty sure the last few seasons of GoT would have been a lot better if GRRM had just said, &quot;the shows are going to be their own things to end in a way that compliments the show instead of worrying about how I plan on ending it.&quot; When GoT's team announced GRRM gave them the outline for the rest of story, and GRRM went so far as to say that if he doesn't finish the books, the shows should be considered canon. That put a lot of pressure on the show to do things that just didn't work right for live action fantasy drama.<br /> <br /> So yeah, TV/film/etc. writers think they can do better than the original creator because frequently they can in the limited scope of adaptations.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-11T20:20:57-07:00","id":1494833,"title":"","content":"I'm honestly surprised there aren't more artists willing to treat any adaptation as a chance to revise, rework, and reimagine their works, and if it turns out this version of Interview is the way it is because Anne Rice decided to take the opportunity to fix what she's dissatisfied with her early stuff now, more power to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-12T00:24:00-07:00","id":1494846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1488888-did-any-of-you-see-the-trailer-for-the-remake-of-anne-rices-s-interview-with-the-vampire?p=1494833#post1494833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm honestly surprised there aren't more artists willing to treat any adaptation as a chance to revise, rework, and reimagine their works, and if it turns out this version of Interview is the way it is because Anne Rice decided to take the opportunity to fix what she's dissatisfied with her early stuff now, more power to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>You do see that, but it's a pretty risky strategy. Companies go for adaptations because there's already a pre-built, existing fan base. So you already have a large (hopefully), sympathetic group of people who will engage positively with the product. But if you change things up too much and deviate too far soon the source, you risk alienating those people, which can end up backfiring pretty badly <br /> <br /> With this adaptation, Anne Rice was involved with the initial outline and direction, though after her untimely death, it's impossible to know how far things deviated. At least though a lot of the basic concepts were approved by her.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-12T09:53:36-07:00","id":1494871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1488888-did-any-of-you-see-the-trailer-for-the-remake-of-anne-rices-s-interview-with-the-vampire?p=1494825#post1494825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're going to do a Louis who loves Lestat, isn't guilty about murder, and tortured by being a monster then why even call Interview with a Vampire?</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't forget the changes to the setting, character backgrounds and so on.<br /> <br /> I am mostly resigned to adaptations being bad or at least wildly changing things. When I want the story I read the original. Because an adaptation is always a different beast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-12T10:58:40-07:00","id":1494876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1488888-did-any-of-you-see-the-trailer-for-the-remake-of-anne-rices-s-interview-with-the-vampire?p=1494833#post1494833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm honestly surprised there aren't more artists willing to treat any adaptation as a chance to revise, rework, and reimagine their works, and if it turns out this version of Interview is the way it is because Anne Rice decided to take the opportunity to fix what she's dissatisfied with her early stuff now, more power to it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Most artists are never sated with there work and know they can always can tweak it. But they acknowledge at some point they have to stop and show it to the world and hope they did well enough with the work. It's why you have actors &amp; actresses who won't watch there work until many years later if at all as they question why they chose to perform that way and not this way and the same can be said of Directors &amp; Producers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-14T17:19:18-07:00","id":1494996,"title":"","content":"for the book purist, i only have to say watch the first 3 episodes and then decide whether its good or not. If you dont like it after 3 episodes then fair enough. Drop it! But the show deserves a chance and this is coming from someone who really wasnt planning on watching this show because of the changes. Its very competently made! This isn ROP, where they butchered the lore by changing it and still made a shit show.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24527-blackshade","name":"blackshade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-15T18:40:22-07:00","id":1495046,"title":"","content":"Going to also urge people that are reluctant to give the show a watch. I'm not sure how everyone can get to watch a behind the scenes featurette that was on AMC but the creators of this show love, love, love the books. They were in constant contact with Anne Rice and her son, who is a very good writer in his own right and very protective of his Mom's work. Multiple people involved cry talking about what reading the books meant to them as a queer kid back when very little was speaking to who they felt they were. <br /> <br /> I get having love for the original books, I have it myself, but so much of it does not age well. A direct adaptation is not possible for a lot of reasons, whether the casting, the storylines that handled sensitive topics very clumsily (they are decades old books to be fair), the drop in quality of later books. Most of all....Anne Rice didn't have a consistent world herself. The Vampire Lestat is a retcon of Interview with the Vampire in so many ways and not just because Lestat gets his POV expressed. It is something the show runners and writers discussed at length when adapting. As the books go on this increasingly becomes a problem. Any of the changes, even large ones like how Daniel is handled as this being set decades after the first interview were done with thought and care, at least so far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27502-caelican","name":"Caelican","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-16T16:34:59-07:00","id":1495089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The idea of being a &quot;purist&quot; for the lore of a non-interactive form of media boggles my mind. Being a purist about RPG lore? OK, I can get that, RPGs are a collaborative media and being a purist about lore is a good way to keep the group on the same page about things. </div> </div> </div>I don't see why you are struggling with it, you already seem to understand the answer when applying it to an RPG. The lore keeps writers making works in that setting on track in regards to how to make a work that belongs in that setting. For an example of what happens when they don't just take a look at The Last Jedi by Rian Johnson. He disregarded the lore of the setting in favor of making the story he wanted to tell and in doing so created massive plot holes that rippled back in time and introduced inconsistencies in already existing works of the setting. The biggest one being 'if using a hyper space jump suicide attack is so ridiculously effective why has nobody ever used them in other stories in the setting or even so much as considered using them? Why didn't the CSA have suicide droids piloting glorified missiles through Republic fleets using hyper space ramming attacks? Why didn't the rebels just have some ships suicide ram the first death star?&quot; and so on and so forth. That is why sticking to the lore is important.<br /> <br /> Of course, that doesn't apply to a reboot. In that case it is basically 'I like it the way it is and the more changes you make the more chances you have to transform it into something I don't like'.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Being a purist about novels just reduces the number of novels in the world. Most novels are the product of someone saying, &quot;I really love story X, but I want to do my version of it instead.&quot; Even people like Tolkien had that as a motivation for all his world building: he wanted to take old stories from his younger years and do his own spin on them. Shakespeare's plays are full of retellings of older stories originally done by someone else. Etc. </div> </div> </div>You will notice that instead of doing something like 'A retelling of Beowulf by Tolkien'* he went out and made a completely new world and story all his own inspired by these older works. The idea that there would be fewer works in the world if people inspired by Tolkien went and made 'the duke of the circles' instead of 'Lord of the Rings as reimagined by random dude guy' is laughable. Very rare seeming is the adaption that makes significant changes while feeling respectful of the work its adapting as opposed to it being a sign they had no faith in an original story putting butts in seats and so hastily spray painted over an unrelated story with an existing popular IP without the slightest care for making it really fit as an adaption of that more popular IP.<br /> <br /> *Yes I know he did do a translation of it from old English to modern English, not the same thing as a re-imagining.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":988,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","user":"Mizu","date":". 10-16-2022, 10:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-16T18:35:56-07:00","id":1495095,"title":"","content":"I've only watched the first, free, episode, but I find that it very much captured the mood of the novel.<br /> <br /> Edit: Okay, watched through episode 4, and it is excellent. A really excellent blend of humor and genuine darkness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3598,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","user":"CajunKhan","date":". 10-17-2022, 01:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-17T10:42:42-07:00","id":1495127,"title":"","content":"Not to mention Mizu that the Star Wars sequals had no real vision compared to the original trilogies and prequals that was the rise, fall and redemption of Anakin Skywalker that George Lucas had in mind. What we got was a muddled mess that turned Han Solo into a deadbeat Dad and left his wife alone to run things and Luke Skywalker the hero of the original trilogy into a bitter surly hermit that wants to die and not even try to stop the First Order and Papaltine is back with no real explaination. I'm reminded by the statement that Ian Malcolm in the first Jurassic Park of how they stood on the shoulders of giants and arrogantly they thought they could do better then the original creators.<br /> <br /> In fact you could go on a tangent of how bad the Star Wars sequals were treated in Kathlyn Kennedy's hands and not find much positive comments of how the stories were done. But I don't want to cause trouble for the moderator on this board and have this thread closed and people getting in trouble.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 10-17-2022, 02:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-17T14:54:05-07:00","id":1495142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1488888-did-any-of-you-see-the-trailer-for-the-remake-of-anne-rices-s-interview-with-the-vampire?p=1495089#post1495089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see why you are struggling with it, you already seem to understand the answer when applying it to an RPG.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought I was pretty clear:<br /> <br /> RPGs are an actively collaborative process. The GM/etc. and the players need to have a baseline agreement on what the setting they're playing in looks like so they can mutually participate in it.<br /> <br /> When I run a VtM game, I need my players to understand the VtM setting on a level; and having a solid lore for the game helps communicate that setting to them.<br /> <br /> If I want to write a short story set in the WoD, I can diverge from the setting canon as much as I want (and WW has repeatedly given novel authors freedom to do exactly that for the sake of evocative stories rather than worrying about forcing the stories to fit to a single continuity), and either other people enjoy it or they don't. There aren't player that have a role in the process that need to understand what events from the books I'm ignoring, or that I'm playing really loose with this rule or that rule, for the sake of the narrative I want to convey.<br /> <br /> If someone is doing an adaptation of an existing work, they're only as beholden to the original as they want to be (including, of course, the potential to want to profit off their work and thus appeal to fans of the exist material by not straying too far). If the work is good, generally speaking for most of human history, nobody gave a shit about taking creative liberties while doing adaptations/reimagings/etc. For most of artistic history taking an existing story, and retelling it in a way people like rather than being &quot;purist&quot; about the origin was a laudable activity. The only place where &quot;purists&quot;had a real argument was in translations because when you're translating there's a serious balancing act of directly translating the body of the work at the risk not the new audience not understanding things that don't communicate well in direct translation vs. translating the spirit of the original while sacrificing some accuracy to it's exact state. Amusingly there are &quot;purists&quot; on both sides of this because there are people that want to be true to the text, and others that want to be true to the narrative; and both groups have people that consider their priority the true &quot;pure&quot; version of the source material.<br /> <br /> The nature of needing consistent lore doesn't apply like it does to RPGs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The lore keeps writers making works in that setting on track in regards to how to make a work that belongs in that setting. </div> </div> </div>According to who? White Wolf green light lots of stories for novels/comics/short stories/etc. for the WoD because they felt the spirit of the stories belonged in the setting even if the specifics of the stories didn't actually work with how the gaming books were written. So clearly there isn't some objective &quot;true&quot; version of the setting to weigh this against. Legally the IP owners get to do this however they want. Fans can disagree, and will voice it loudly if they do, but fans saying that a wok doesn't belong in the setting doesn't define things with any real authority.<br /> <br /> Lots of franchises eschew your concept of setting purity for numerous reasons. In the end, works get judged far more on quality than on setting purism (esp. considering nobody can even agree about literal purism vs. narrative purism).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For an example of what happens when they don't just take a look at The Last Jedi by Rian Johnson. </div> </div> </div>You're talking about Star Wars. The franchise that at one point - under George Lucas mind you - has a six tiered canon classification system to sort which sources to give precedence to because George Lucas notoriously (and quite explicitly) did not give two shits about how the EU folks followed his canon or not. Do you realize how big of a mess the old EU was if it needed six different levels of canon in order to figure out whether or not an event &quot;happened&quot; one way or another if you want your future stories to comply with one level of canon instead of falling into a lower tier of canon?<br /> <br /> And canon tier was no indicator of quality. The G-Canon, the tippy top George Lucas stamp of approval canon, including every last still hated moment of the prequel trilogy, while much beloved material like some of the video games and comics are stuck at the 3rd,4th or even 6th level of canon (the sixth being non-canon including things that were originally S or C canon but the prequels rendered them N canon as Lucas didn't care if his stories made fan favorites stories incompatible with the G canon). <br /> <br /> So yeah, spare me the idea that &quot;purists&quot; are what keeps stories good. There were bad SW stories of high tier canon, and good SW stories of low tier canon, well before Disney got in the picture. Or at least make me a good argument that G and T canon are clearly superior to S and C canon in SW simply because those tiers are about &quot;purity&quot; to Lucas's vision and not anything else (very literally according to the man himself, it's only about what matches his vision of the setting and what strays from it).<br /> <br /> I don't care about getting into a debate about the flaws of one entry in the SW franchise, but the sheer amount of stuff people seem to love to forget was in the old stories never ceases to amaze me. For every flaw you can find in the sequel trilogy, I can point out a dozen in the material put out in the old Lucas days (hey remember when SW had a fighter sized space ship that could fly into a sun and cause it to go nova and survive, and then everyone acted like since the prototype was destroyed it was impossible for that to ever be a problem ever again? I do, so I can get past hyper-space ramming and nobody following up on that). Star Wars was never about high art and strong setting consistency, it was about cool iconic action fantasy stories in space; and the creatives that have worked on it over the decades have all understood that was more important than worrying about there being three different origin stories of Boba Fett out there (and if you think &quot;guy making a kid clone of himself to raise as a son&quot; is the best, and the best fit for the rest of the Mandolarian stuff... I have no idea what to say to that).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Very rare seeming is the adaption that makes significant changes while feeling respectful of the work its adapting as opposed to it being a sign they had no faith in an original story putting butts in seats and so hastily spray painted over an unrelated story with an existing popular IP without the slightest care for making it really fit as an adaption of that more popular IP. </div> </div> </div>Or, you know, it's just the elevation of &quot;fandom&quot; as a thing that really matters, and thus needs to be catered to. Fans are the source of this perception. I say this as an avid fan of many things. Look at me go on about WoD5... that's only happening because of how attached I am emotionally to the older stuff. I can try my best to come up with as many objective or rational reasons for what I'm saying and why it should matter, but in the end Paradox doesn't need to care, and I have no claim to say they have to care. The quality of the WoD5 books isn't going to be judged by history on how much they listened to fans like me vs. other fans. At best we might be considered people that read the room right. We'll have no more importance than that.<br /> <br /> Seriously, if you look at any form of art it's the fans (or various other &quot;insiders&quot; that came before) that make a big deal about this,not anyone else. Because fans are the people that care about this sort of &quot;literal purist&quot; respect for previous works. Most people just want a story that matches the mood they're in, and if it positively reminds them of works they liked before? Even better.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yes I know he did do a translation of it from old English to modern English, not the same thing as a re-imagining. </div> </div> </div>Linguists, of which he was one, would definitely disagree that you can do a translation that doesn't also count as a reimaging on some level. As is frequently said: &quot;translation is interpretation.&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-17T15:19:38-07:00","id":1495144,"title":"","content":"One man's enjoyment of a carefully held series of events and interpretations is another's cage of boredom. Personally, if it's a choice between precious continuity and interesting ideas, I'd rather burn the canon.<br /> <br /> (Star Wars is <i>entirely</i> the reason that's the case, and that was true before the Disney purchase. It is the <i>wrong</i> franchise to get precious about.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 10-17-2022, 06:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-17T19:28:18-07:00","id":1495150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1488888-did-any-of-you-see-the-trailer-for-the-remake-of-anne-rices-s-interview-with-the-vampire?p=1495127#post1495127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not to mention Mizu that the Star Wars sequals had no real vision compared to the original trilogies and prequals that was the rise, fall and redemption of Anakin Skywalker that George Lucas had in mind. What we got was a muddled mess that turned Han Solo into a deadbeat Dad and left his wife alone to run things and Luke Skywalker the hero of the original trilogy into a bitter surly hermit that wants to die and not even try to stop the First Order and Papaltine is back with no real explaination. I'm reminded by the statement that Ian Malcolm in the first Jurassic Park of how they stood on the shoulders of giants and arrogantly they thought they could do better then the original creators.<br /> <br /> <b>In fact you could go on a tangent of how bad the Star Wars sequals were treated in Kathlyn Kennedy's hands and not find much positive comments of how the stories were done. But I don't want to cause trouble for the moderator on this board and have this thread closed and people getting in trouble.</b></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b>Then probably best not to say it.<br /> <br /> Just saying.</b></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&a